From 9f8748f30560d681245d9bf7b788b687683307dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:12:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: diagnostics plugin hook API and loader

Diagnostics move out of the engine into an optional plugin library. This patch
adds the seam: one PS2DiagHooks pointer, null = no plugin (a play build), one
load and null check per hook site, same pattern as PS2ExternalGS/PS2ExternalVu1.
The in-engine diagnostics stay until the next patch removes them.

- runtime/ps2_diag_hooks.h (light header, versioned PS2_DIAG_API_VERSION 1):
  PS2DiagHost (apiVersion, sizeof(VU1State), readGuest, vsyncTick) and
  PS2DiagHooks: onVsync(tick, idleWaitNs), wantsFrame(tick), onGuestEnter(pc*,
  tid)/onGuestLeave, onSectionEnter/Leave (Vu1, Iop, Gs, GsVsync),
  onVu1Begin/onVu1Path1/onVu1End, onRunEnd (scheduler thread); padButtons
  (game thread); onFrame, onHostFrame (0 go on, 1 stop, >=2 exit code),
  onShutdown (main thread). PS2DiagSectionScope for hot paths.
- src/lib/ps2_diag.cpp: ps2LoadDiagPlugin loads PS2X_DIAG=<path>, else
  <exe dir>/<PS2X_DIAG_NAME>.dll|.so if present (CMake cache, default ob_diag);
  entry ps2_diag_create(host, &exitCode): null + 0 = nothing to do, null + code
  = exit with it. A named plugin that does not load = exit 2.
- Hook sites: scheduler (VBlankStart onVsync after the script step and before
  the snapshot decision; pacing wait summed when a plugin is loaded; guest
  enter/leave; run end), GIF arbiter (Gs), VU1 interpreter run (Vu1) and
  finishXgkick (Path1), runtime IOP calls (Iop), VIF1 MSCAL/MSCNT callbacks
  (begin/end, both VU1 backends), pad poll, UploadFrame (onFrame; the external
  GS frame demand includes wantsFrame), the host loop and its end. Initialize
  fills the host and loads the plugin after the GS/VU1 selection.

Tests: recording hooks see one onVsync per VBlankStart with a cumulative idle
wait and the running context's pc; wantsFrame picks the one external GS
snapshot, GS packet and vsync sections pair up; a pad-owning plugin replaces
the host pad; an MSCAL run reports begin, its PATH1 packet inside the VU1
section, and end; the loader returns 0 with nothing to load and 2 for a
missing PS2X_DIAG.
